Mt-KaHyPar c95e871f: get_node_with_minimum_weighted_degree (the processor
of the seed block in the greedy one-to-one mapping) filters the free
processors by the individual block weights and indexes the candidate
list with a random integer in [0, size - 1].  From the second V-cycle of
mt_kahypar_improve_mapping on, a block can outweigh every processor still
free (the previous cycle's mapping and refinement may leave a block above
its processor's capacity, and the processors of fixed blocks are taken),
the list is empty and uniform_int_distribution(0, -1) recurses until the
stack overflows (SIGSEGV; X5 ethernet_ar1_nangate45, level 4).  Fall back
to the free processors regardless of their capacity, as the main loop of
compute_greedy_mapping already does for the other blocks.

